  "question": "I'm trying to use `BootstrapFinetune` on a tiny offline program before I swap in a real provider. Plain inference works if I only do `dspy.configure(lm=...)`, so I expected the optimizer to inherit that and start compiling.\n\nWhat I'm actually seeing is that compilation fails because one of the predictors supposedly has no LM assigned, even though the global LM is set and the same module can answer questions. I want a proof that this is about per-predictor wiring, not about the dataset or the metric.\n\nGive me a complete, runnable Python program that uses `DummyLM`, triggers the optimizer error first, then fixes it by attaching the LM directly to the module, with prints and assertions that prove the before/after behavior.",
  "answer": "```python\nimport dspy\nfrom unittest.mock import patch\nfrom dspy.teleprompt import BootstrapFinetune\nfrom dspy.utils.dummies import DummyLM\n\n\nclass SimpleModule(dspy.Module):\n    def __init__(self):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.predictor = dspy.Predict(\"input -> output\")\n\n    def forward(self, input):\n        return self.predictor(input=input)\n\n\ndef metric(example, prediction, trace=None):\n    return example.output == prediction.output\n\n\ntrainset = [\n    dspy.Example(input=\"What is the color of the sky?\", output=\"blue\").with_inputs(\"input\")\n]\nlm = DummyLM({\"What is the color of the sky?\": {\"output\": \"blue\"}})\ndspy.configure(lm=lm)\noptimizer = BootstrapFinetune(metric=metric)\nstudent = SimpleModule()\n\nplain_prediction = student(input=\"What is the color of the sky?\")\nprint(\"plain_inference_output:\", plain_prediction.output)\nassert plain_prediction.output == \"blue\"\nassert student.predictor.lm is None\nprint(\"predictor_lm_before_compile:\", student.predictor.lm)\n\ntry:\n    optimizer.compile(student, trainset=trainset)\n    raise AssertionError(\"Expected BootstrapFinetune to reject a predictor that only relies on dspy.configure(lm=...)\")\nexcept ValueError as e:\n    msg = str(e)\n    print(\"missing_lm_error:\", msg)\n    assert \"does not have an LM assigned\" in msg\n    assert \"set_lm\" in msg\n\nassert student.predictor.lm is None\nstudent.set_lm(lm)\nassert student.predictor.lm is lm\nprint(\"predictor_lm_after_set_lm:\", student.predictor.lm.model)\n\nwith patch.object(optimizer, \"finetune_lms\", return_value={(lm, None): lm}) as mocked:\n    compiled = optimizer.compile(student, trainset=trainset)\n    mocked.assert_called_once()\n    assert set(mocked.call_args.args[0]) == {(lm, None)}\n\nassert compiled is student\nassert compiled._compiled is True\nassert compiled.predictor.lm is lm\nprint(\"compiled_flag:\", compiled._compiled)\nprint(\"predictor_lm_model:\", compiled.predictor.lm.model)\n```",
